### Paperless DMS - REST API Tests (Class 4: Custom Use-Case - Document Status & History)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081/api

### 1. Upload a document to start lifecycle (Initial status will be RECEIVED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Invoice for Status Tracking
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample-documents/sample.pdf
--WebAppBoundary--

### 2. Retrieve Document to verify initial status (RECEIVED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/1
Accept: application/json

### 3. Retrieve Status History for the Document (should contain initial upload entry)
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/1/history
Accept: application/json

### 4. Transition Document Status: RECEIVED -> PROCESSING
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PROCESSING",
  "changedBy": "ocr-worker",
  "comment": "Starting OCR text extraction"
}

### 5. Transition Document Status: PROCESSING -> REVIEW_PENDING
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "REVIEW_PENDING",
  "changedBy": "ocr-worker",
  "comment": "OCR extraction completed, pending user review"
}

### 6. Transition Document Status: REVIEW_PENDING -> COMPLETED (Approved)
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "COMPLETED",
  "changedBy": "david.kedra",
  "comment": "Document verified and approved"
}

### 7. Retrieve Complete Status Audit Trail (chronological descending)
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/1/history
Accept: application/json

### 8. Attempt Illegal Status Transition: COMPLETED -> PROCESSING (Should return 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PROCESSING",
  "changedBy": "hacker",
  "comment": "Illegal jump from COMPLETED"
}

### 9. Retrieve Specific History Entry by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/status-history/1
Accept: application/json
